      "type": "item",
      "section": "Compute, chips & infrastructure",
      "headline": "FT: technology companies provided as much as $300 billion in guarantees financing AI data centres and chips",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Staying with the money. Seeking Alpha, summarising the Financial Times, reports technology companies have provided as much as $300 billion in guarantees to finance AI data centers and chips during the past year." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "And most of that isn't recorded as debt?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "That's the point of the structure. The guarantee promises a minimum asset value through a special-purpose arrangement, so the capacity gets added without the exposure landing immediately as debt on the guarantor's books." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "What's the risk in that?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Seeking Alpha writes that the guarantees can obscure potential liabilities if demand fails or equipment devalues, and that losses would rise if AI hardware becomes obsolete quickly or the industry overbuilds capacity." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "We could not open the Financial Times piece itself, so only the figures printed on the Seeking Alpha page are reported, and that single source is what this rests on. Company-level breakdowns circulating elsewhere aren't in our edition, because we didn't read them in the original." }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "transition", "lines": [ { "host": "A", "text": "Last stretch. Deployment, and what it is doing to people." } ] },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "section": "Deployment & impact",
      "headline": "New York Times: DraftKings scored bettors by expected losses and aimed about $400 million of promotions at them",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "The New York Times published an investigation on September 19th into DraftKings. We're reading it through Tech Times, because the Times itself wouldn't open for us." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "What did they find?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "A machine-learning model built in 2023 that scored each online casino player by how much they were expected to lose after getting a free bet or a bonus. It weighed play frequency, daily account balances, and the ratio of losses to wagers. Staff called the output an elasticity score." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "And how much money moved on the back of it?" },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Roughly $400 million in automated promotions aimed at the highest-scoring accounts in 2025. Executives credit data science and personalised promotions with lifting the sportsbook margin by 13 percent that year." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "There's a second model in this story, though." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "There is. Former employees said a parallel model meant to flag customers sliding toward gambling harm, started by a data scientist in 2024, was shelved. The chief responsible gaming officer said leadership decided against predictive risk tools because the approach was not evidence-based." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "DraftKings says it rejects any implication that its marketing is unfair, and that promotions go to customers showing sustained, engaged use of the platform, not to customers picked out by their losses. All of this traces back to a single source, one Times investigation." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "section": "Deployment & impact",
      "headline": "Flock Safety offers voluntary buyouts across its 1,500-person workforce after surveillance backlash",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "Flock Safety is offering voluntary buyouts across its 1,500-person workforce." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "TechCrunch, reporting on a Wired story, says the packages were announced on Friday and described internally as the most generous the company has ever offered. Flock expects a significant portion of staff to express interest, and said that without the buyouts it would almost certainly need to lay people off." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Why is the company under this much pressure?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "TechCrunch cites 46 documented cases of police officers misusing Flock's licence plate recognition technology, Florida and Texas halting use of the system, and 90 cities terminating Flock contracts in August alone, four times the previous month." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Chief executive Garrett Langley said the biggest damage from the backlash has been to internal morale. The story originates with Wired, it's a single source, and no headcount reduction target has been published." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "section": "Deployment & impact",
      "headline": "AI evaluation startup Vals raises a $40 million Series A led by Andreessen Horowitz",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "One funding round worth your time. TechCrunch reports Vals, an AI evaluation startup founded in 2024, raised a $40 million Series A led by Andreessen Horowitz." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "What do they actually sell?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Model developers pay Vals to test their models. Co-founder Rayan Krishnan compares it to students paying for the SAT. They evaluate on law, finance and coding tasks, and they're extending into recursive self-improvement, mental health, cybersecurity, biosecurity and the law of armed conflict." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "And they've started selling to government." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "They recently launched a programme providing model evaluations to federal agencies. Headcount went from 8 at the start of the year to 25, with 10 to 15 more planned, and revenue is 8 times last year's." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Those last figures are the company's own numbers, a company claim, not independently verified. And Vals doesn't publish its test materials, to stop models being trained against them, which also means the scores can't be reproduced by anyone outside. One outlet has this." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "That's The AI Edge for today." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "The full edition is on the site, with a link to every source behind every claim we've made. Nothing in this episode goes further than what's written there." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "A quiet weekend for the labs and for arXiv. A loud one for Washington." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Listen in tomorrow for the next edition." }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

